<!-- SECTION: contribute.Contribute — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="Contribute — title"><h1><span class="u-1">Contribute</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>Back the work directly.</h2>
  <p>Money is not the only way in — and right now it isn&rsquo;t even open yet. The most useful things you can give today are time, skills, and in-kind resources. Here&rsquo;s exactly what that looks like.</p>
</div>
<!-- SECTION: contribute.Status -->
<div class="statusband" data-screen-label="Status">
  <span class="status status--planned">Donations not open</span>
  <span>Uncost is seeking fiscal sponsorship before accepting public donations. You can register an intention to give now, and we&rsquo;ll contact you when it opens — no money changes hands today.</span>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: contribute.Three ways -->
<div class="ways" data-screen-label="Three ways">
  <div class="way">
    <h3>Give</h3><div class="tag">When donations open</div>
    <ul><li>Register an intention to give — we&rsquo;ll email you the moment donations lawfully open.</li><li>One-time or recurring, once the sponsor structure is confirmed.</li><li>Every dollar will be reported in The Treasury.</li></ul>
    <a href="/pledge/" class="u-btn u-btn--primary btn">Register intent — sign the Pledge</a>
  </div>
  <div class="way">
    <h3>Volunteer</h3><div class="tag">Time &amp; skills</div>
    <ul><li>The fastest way to move the evidence forward.</li><li>Source and license review are the first roles we need.</li><li>Remote, flexible, credited in the public record.</li></ul>
    <a href="/contact/" class="u-btn u-btn--ink btn">Tell us how you can help</a>
  </div>
  <div class="way">
    <h3>In-kind</h3><div class="tag">Resources &amp; compute</div>
    <ul><li>Compute, model access, and software credits.</li><li>Equipment, data access, logistics, storage.</li><li>Treated as first-class support — it lowers the cost of building Uncost itself.</li></ul>
    <a href="/contact/" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost btn">Offer in-kind support</a>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: contribute.Volunteer roles -->
<section class="blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="Volunteer roles">
  <div class="eyebrow">Where volunteers help first</div>
  <h2 class="u-42 sec">Useful roles, right now.</h2>
  <div class="roles">
    <div class="role"><b>Source &amp; license review</b><span>Check that every figure has a real, licensed, dated source before it publishes.</span></div>
    <div class="role"><b>Data methodology</b><span>Help design how costs are measured, compared, and refreshed by region.</span></div>
    <div class="role"><b>Sector research</b><span>Write and maintain a sector dossier: scope, opportunity, guardrails.</span></div>
    <div class="role"><b>Engineering</b><span>Build the open tools — dashboards, trackers, and the data pipelines behind them.</span></div>
    <div class="role"><b>Content &amp; design</b><span>Turn sourced evidence into short, honest, shareable explainers.</span></div>
    <div class="role"><b>Translation &amp; moderation</b><span>Widen who can take part, and keep the community constructive.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="u-43">Some volunteer roles may later become paid roles if funding allows — volunteering doesn&rsquo;t guarantee employment or retroactive pay, and we&rsquo;ll always say so plainly.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: contribute.Contribute CTA -->
